        "By bounding inputs, the testing surface becomes finite, enabling more thorough testing, fuzzing, and formal verification of MODEXP implementations.",
        "Historical consensus bugs from impractical/extreme input lengths are prevented by the new bound.",
        "The EIP-198 pricing function complexity (driven by unbounded inputs) may be simplified in a future upgrade once the limits are in place.",
        "The bounded input range facilitates a future replacement of the MODEXP precompile with EVM code through features like EVMMAX, because common cases (256, 381, 1024, 2048 bits) can be implemented as fast paths with a slow fallback for the rest.",
